## Programme

We start with three short talks, and then it's over to you. In groups, you write down the
challenges you run into on the Discussion form, then read and rate what the other groups came up
with on the Review form. We finish together with the issues you rated highest, and your questions.

<!-- md:replace programme -->
<Programme rows={superAgentProgramme} />
<!-- md:end -->

## Outcomes

Questions we hope to answer together.

1. Which frictions are blocking researchers from getting work done on shared HPC?
2. What should HPC providers pick up next, and what useful practices can researchers share with
   each other in the meantime?
3. As agents take over cluster work, will researchers still need cluster knowledge, and who debugs
   it when the agent gets it wrong?

Everything the groups write down ends up on the board below, and your ratings sort it into low,
medium, and high impact. In the plenary we go through the high-impact issues together. The board
fills up during the session, so it's worth keeping an eye on.

